From 1b251442a74498bf499faf0c3e0f599cfcc0deb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:51:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updates: say where the versions of LibreELEC Hades are
 published

LibreELEC Hades has no update channel: its update URLs are empty, so that
the update server of LibreELEC, whose builds would replace this one, is
never asked. "Available Versions" said only that there was no channel and
to copy an update file to the Update folder, without saying where one
comes from; and the help of "Automatic updates" was LibreELEC's, which
says that automatic updates are available on stable releases.

Now "Available Versions" names the page where the versions are published
(https://github.com/hadesdevls/LibreELEC-Hades/releases), which file
updates a system (the one whose name ends in .tar), where it goes (the
Update folder, shared on the network as "Update" when file sharing is on)
and that the installer for Windows published with it can update the drive
as well. While there is no channel, the help of "Automatic updates" says
that nothing is looked for or downloaded by itself, whatever is chosen,
and names the same page. Nothing is looked for or downloaded because of
this change, and a build with an update channel keeps LibreELEC's help.

Texts in English, and in Spanish for Spain, Argentina and Mexico.
